From 04a351074d4fe84dbf67d03622377b270e47f856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:04:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A console clock for the visual check: `worldclock <minute>`
 holds the time of day

`worldclock 1050` holds the world's light at 17:30 (any minute of the game day, 0 to 1439, 720
noon), as the debug panel's clock scrub does; `worldclock server`, or `worldclock` alone, follows
the server's clock again. It is for the scripted visual check, whose scenarios shoot Elwynn at a
set hour with `ConsoleExec("worldclock 1050")`: the light, the sky and the new look's grade follow
on the next frame, and the server's own clock is untouched. A minute out of range or a word that
is not one prints the usage line and changes nothing. benilla's own; 1.12 has no such command.

`lookbloom <intensity> [threshold]` holds the new look's bloom the same way, so one take can
compare several; `lookbloom grade`, or no argument, lets the hour's grade decide again.

`lookmist <scale>` holds the mist at a multiple of the hour's own (0 to 6), and `lookmist grade`
lets go.
---
 crates/benilla-app/src/world_console.rs | 214 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 214 insertions(+)

